#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:25
msgid ""
"In a :doc:`previous tutorial <Custom-ROS2-Interfaces>`, you learned how to "
"create custom msg and srv interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:27
msgid ""
"While best practice is to declare interfaces in dedicated interface "
"packages, sometimes it can be convenient to declare, create and use an "
"interface all in one package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:29
msgid ""
"Recall that interfaces can currently only be defined in CMake packages. It "
"is possible, however, to have Python libraries and nodes in CMake packages "
"(using `ament_cmake_python <https://github.com/ament/ament_cmake/tree/"
"rolling/ament_cmake_python>`_), so you could define interfaces and Python "
"nodes together in one package. We'll use a CMake package and C++ nodes here "
"for the sake of simplicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:33
msgid ""
"This tutorial will focus on the msg interface type, but the steps here are "
"applicable to all interface types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:36
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "先備條件"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:38
msgid ""
"We assume you've reviewed the basics in the :doc:`Custom-ROS2-Interfaces` "
"tutorial before working through this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:40
msgid ""
"You should have :doc:`ROS 2 installed <../../../Get-Started/Installation>`, "
"a :doc:`workspace <Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace>`, and an "
"understanding of :doc:`creating packages <Creating-Your-First-ROS2-Package>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:42
msgid ""
"As always, don't forget to :doc:`source ROS 2 <../../../Get-Started/"
"Configuring-ROS2-Environment>` in every new terminal you open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:45
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:48
msgid "1 Create a package"
msgstr "1 建立軟體包"

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:50
msgid ""
"In your workspace ``src`` directory, create a package ``more_interfaces`` "
"and make a directory within it for msg files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:52
msgid ""
"$ ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_cmake --license Apache-2.0 "
"more_interfaces\n"
"$ mkdir more_interfaces/msg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:58
msgid "2 Create a msg file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:60
msgid ""
"Inside ``more_interfaces/msg``, create a new file ``AddressBook.msg``, and "
"paste the following code to create a message meant to carry information "
"about an individual:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:64
msgid ""
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_HOME=0\n"
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_WORK=1\n"
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_MOBILE=2\n"
"\n"
"string first_name\n"
"string last_name\n"
"string phone_number\n"
"uint8 phone_type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:73
msgid "This message is composed of these fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:75
msgid "first_name: of type string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:76
msgid "last_name: of type string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:77
msgid "phone_number: of type string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:78
msgid "phone_type: of type uint8, with several named constant values defined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:80
msgid ""
"Note that it's possible to set default values for fields within a message "
"definition. See :doc:`../../interfaces/About-Interfaces` for more ways you "
"can customize interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:83
msgid ""
"Next, we need to make sure that the msg file is turned into source code for "
"C++, Python, and other languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:86
msgid "2.1 Build a msg file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:88
msgid "Open ``package.xml`` and add the following lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:90
msgid ""
"<buildtool_depend>rosidl_default_generators</buildtool_depend>\n"
"\n"
"<exec_depend>rosidl_default_runtime</exec_depend>\n"
"\n"
"<member_of_group>rosidl_interface_packages</member_of_group>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:98
msgid ""
"Note that at build time, we need ``rosidl_default_generators``, while at "
"runtime, we only need ``rosidl_default_runtime``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:100
msgid "Open ``CMakeLists.txt`` and add the following lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:102
msgid "Find the package that generates message code from msg/srv files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:104
msgid "find_package(rosidl_default_generators REQUIRED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:108
msgid "Declare the list of messages you want to generate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:110
msgid ""
"set(msg_files\n"
"  \"msg/AddressBook.msg\"\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:116
msgid ""
"By adding the .msg files manually, we make sure that CMake knows when it has "
"to reconfigure the project after you add other .msg files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:118
msgid "Generate the messages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:120
msgid ""
"rosidl_generate_interfaces(${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
"  ${msg_files}\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:126
msgid "Also make sure you export the message runtime dependency:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:128
msgid "ament_export_dependencies(rosidl_default_runtime)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:132
msgid ""
"Now you're ready to generate source files from your msg definition. We'll "
"skip the compile step for now as we'll do it all together below in step 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:136
msgid "3 Use an interface from the same package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:138
msgid "Now we can start writing code that uses this message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:140
msgid ""
"In ``more_interfaces/src`` create a file called ``publish_address_book.cpp`` "
"and paste the following code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:142
msgid ""
"#include <chrono>\n"
"#include <memory>\n"
"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\"\n"
"#include \"more_interfaces/msg/address_book.hpp\"\n"
"\n"
"using namespace std::chrono_literals;\n"
"\n"
"class AddressBookPublisher : public rclcpp::Node\n"
"{\n"
"public:\n"
"  AddressBookPublisher()\n"
"  : Node(\"address_book_publisher\")\n"
"  {\n"
"    address_book_publisher_ =\n"
"      this->create_publisher<more_interfaces::msg::"
"AddressBook>(\"address_book\", 10);\n"
"\n"
"    auto publish_msg = [this]() -> void {\n"
"        auto message = more_interfaces::msg::AddressBook();\n"
"\n"
"        message.first_name = \"John\";\n"
"        message.last_name = \"Doe\";\n"
"        message.phone_number = \"1234567890\";\n"
"        message.phone_type = message.PHONE_TYPE_MOBILE;\n"
"\n"
"        std::cout << \"Publishing Contact\\nFirst:\" << message.first_name "
"<<\n"
"          \"  Last:\" << message.last_name << std::endl;\n"
"\n"
"        this->address_book_publisher_->publish(message);\n"
"      };\n"
"    timer_ = this->create_wall_timer(1s, publish_msg);\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"private:\n"
"  rclcpp::Publisher<more_interfaces::msg::AddressBook>::SharedPtr "
"address_book_publisher_;\n"
"  rclcpp::TimerBase::SharedPtr timer_;\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char * argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"  rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"  rclcpp::spin(std::make_shared<AddressBookPublisher>());\n"
"  rclcpp::shutdown();\n"
"\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:193
msgid "3.1 The code explained"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:195
msgid "Include the header of our newly created ``AddressBook.msg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:197
